            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="0959" n="869" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg869"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2224: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Spencer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-23T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>50. Department has received despatch from American Consul at Tegucigalpa dated
                    September l,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d788-f1"/> reporting that revolutionists have
                        <pb facs="0960" n="870" xml:id="pg870"/> entered Honduranian territory from
                    both the Nicaraguan and Salvadorean borders and have apparently made
                    arrangements for uprisings to take place in Choluteca and other cities. Please
                    cable brief report stating whether such uprisings have occurred and if so,
                    whether there is any probability that the movement will become general in
                    character.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
